    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32016" root="غضو and غضى" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَضْيَآءُ</span></b>  A land (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْضٌ</span>) <i>abounding with the trees
called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَضًا</span>. (S, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And, as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَضْيَا</span></b> , <i>A
place in which is a collection of the trees called</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَضًا</span>; (K, TA;) <i>a place where they grow.</i> (TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And the former, <i>Rugged</i> land or ground.
(TA.)

